 Creating a complex smart contract involves writing a self-executing program on a blockchain network that automates the execution of certain conditions and actions. Here's an example of a smart contract written in Solidity, a popular programming language for Ethereum:

```solidity
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

contract ComplexContract {
    struct User {
        address payable address;
        uint256 balance;
    }

    User[] public users;

    constructor() public {
        // Initialize users with their initial balances
        users.push(User({address: msg.sender, balance: 1000}));
    }

    function deposit() public payable {
        // Check if the sender is a registered user
        require(users[msg.sender].address == msg.sender, "You must be a registered user to deposit.");

        // Add the deposited amount to the user's balance
        users[msg.sender].balance += msg.value;
    }

    function withdraw(uint256 amount) public {
        // Check if the sender has enough balance to withdraw
        require(users[msg.sender].balance >= amount, "Insufficient balance to withdraw.");

        // Withdraw the specified amount from the user's balance
        users[msg.sender].balance -= amount;

        // Send the withdrawn amount to the sender's Ethereum address
        msg.sender.transfer(amount);
    }

    function transfer(address payable recipient, uint256 amount) public {
        // Check if the sender has enough balance to transfer
        require(users[msg.sender].balance >= amount, "Insufficient balance to transfer.");

        // Transfer the specified amount from the sender's balance to the recipient's address
        users[msg.sender].balance -= amount;
        recipient.transfer(amount);
    }
}
```

This smart contract allows users to deposit, withdraw, and transfer Ether (ETH) while maintaining a balance for each user. It also includes error handling to ensure that users can't perform actions they're not allowed to do, such as withdrawing more Ether than they have or transferring Ether to an address with insufficient balance.

